{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "9ea50c34-2361-4201-a421-43c9fc1999e4",
  "Description": "All seven MediaPipe operators in one graph, sharing a single camera: hand, pose and face landmark detection, face and object detection, gesture recognition and image segmentation. The [Index] input of [PickTexture] selects which operator's debug view is shown:\n\n0 = Image segmentation (mask tint via [BlendWithMask])\n1 = Gesture recognition\n2 = Object detection\n3 = Face detection\n4 = Face landmark detection\n5 = Pose landmark detection\n6 = Hand landmark detection\n\nOnly the operator currently selected by [Index] runs on the camera image each frame; its outputs (point buffers, counts, gesture names, masks) are available while it is selected, and the unselected operators cost no CPU until selected. See the individual *Example operators for a description of each operator's inputs and outputs.\n\n[Acceleration] is Xnnpack everywhere; running several of these models in one graph is heavy, so keep [Index] on the operator you currently need.",
